    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n35238" root="قد" body-key="q">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">قَيْدُودٌ</span></b>  A she-camel <i>long in the back:</i> (O, K:)
but this is said to be derived from <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">القَوْدُ</span>, like
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">الكَيْنُونَةُ</span> from <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">الكَوْنُ</span>: (L:) [see art. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">قود</span>:] pl.
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">قَيَادِيدُ</span>. (K. [In the O the pl. is written <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">قَنَادِيدُ</span>.])

